SiraGPT — SiraCode notice
=========================

SiraCode is the native coding-agent core in this repository
(`backend/src/services/sira-code/`). It is an independent rewrite
inspired by the architecture of OpenCode:

  https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) the OpenCode / Anomaly contributors

MIT allows use of the ideas. This tree does **not** copy the
anomalyco/opencode monorepo (packages/opencode, SST console, Nix,
desktop, Electron, TUI, or the 75-provider catalog). Session titles
are a native rewrite of the ensureTitle idea (first real user
message, once); they are not generated by OpenCode's title agent.
Tool-result caps and transcript prune are a native rewrite of
Truncate / SessionCompaction.prune (lines + bytes, keep the tail);
they do not copy the Effect service or write a tool-output directory.
The reconnect summary is a native rewrite of the SessionSummary idea
(compact snapshot + lastEventId for SSE resume); it does not copy
the Effect service, Snapshot git-diff, or an LLM summarizer.

SiraGPT and SiraCode are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
sponsored by OpenCode or Anomaly.

Third-party architecture notes also live in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
